================================================================================
NAME
       envelopes - envelope shaping, spectral sculpting, and envelope-pattern
                   interaction in RTT

SYNOPSIS
       Envelopes define:
           • spectral shape
           • resonance distribution
           • harmonic emphasis
           • pattern suitability
           • overlay responsiveness

DESCRIPTION
       Envelopes describe the *shape* of resonance-time energy across the
       frequency spectrum. While frequency identifies spectral components and
       harmonics describe oscillatory modes, envelopes describe how resonance
       energy is *sculpted* across those components.

       Envelope shaping determines:
           • which patterns remain stable
           • how overlays behave
           • how resonance propagates
           • how triads evolve across cycles
           • how multi-agent systems synchronize

       Envelopes are computed from spectral snapshots and lineage history.

ENVELOPE TYPES
       narrowband envelope
              Energy concentrated around a single frequency.
              → stable, predictable
              → sequential, core, weave patterns

       broadband envelope
              Energy spread across many frequencies.
              → adaptive, dynamic
              → spiral, ladder, expansion patterns

       multimodal envelope
              Multiple peaks at distinct frequencies.
              → hybrid or fused patterns
              → constellation behavior

       harmonic-clustered envelope
              Peaks at integer multiples.
              → harmonic-sync networks
              → multi-agent coupling

       noise-rich envelope
              High spectral noise; unstable.
              → requires anchor or mirror overlays

ENVELOPE SHAPING
       Envelope shaping is the process of adjusting spectral distribution to
       maintain coherence and pattern stability.

       Shaping techniques:

           damping
                  Reduces high-frequency noise; stabilizes triads.

           boosting
                  Emphasizes specific harmonic bands; supports ladders.

           smoothing
                  Reduces abrupt spectral transitions; prevents drift.

           gating
                  Restricts resonance to allowed spectral regions.

           sculpting
                  Complex shaping across multiple bands; used in hybrid
                  patterns and constellations.

       WRSADC applies shaping automatically when thresholds are approached.

SPECTRAL SCULPTING
       Spectral sculpting is advanced envelope shaping that modifies the
       entire spectral profile to match structural or pattern requirements.

       Sculpting operations:

           carve
                  Remove unwanted spectral regions.

           contour
                  Shape resonance to match pattern geometry.

           layer
                  Combine multiple envelopes into a composite structure.

           braid
                  Interleave spectral bands; used in weave and constellation
                  patterns.

           cascade
                  Apply shaping sequentially across triads.

       Sculpting is guided by schemas and resonance signatures.

ENVELOPES AND TRIADS
       Triads sample and update envelopes at each phase:

           P1 (begin)
               → capture envelope baseline

           P2 (transform)
               → operator resonance signatures reshape envelope

           P3 (close)
               → envelope integrated into lineage

       Envelope evolution determines triadic stability.

ENVELOPES AND PATTERNS
       Patterns require specific envelope shapes:

           sequential
                  narrowband, low noise

           spiral
                  broadband with rising harmonic content

           ladder
                  clustered harmonics with stable peaks

           expansion
                  multimodal, high-frequency spread

           weave
                  interleaved spectral bands

           constellation
                  multi-agent harmonic clusters

       Pattern morphing often corresponds to envelope transitions.

ENVELOPES AND OVERLAYS
       Overlays modify envelope shape:

           telescope
                  Expands or contracts envelope width.

           mirror
                  Inverts spectral distribution.

           anchor
                  Dampens noise; stabilizes envelope.

           lens
                  Reframes spectral interpretation; shifts emphasis.

       Overlay stacks produce composite envelope effects.

ENVELOPES IN MULTI-AGENT CONSTELLATIONS
       Constellations require envelope compatibility:

           • shared envelope shape
           • harmonic alignment
           • stable multimodal structure
           • compatible spectral sculpting rules

       Envelope divergence leads to desync or fragmentation.

ENVELOPE FAILURE MODES
       drift
              Envelope shifts unpredictably across cycles.

       fragmentation
              Envelope splits into incoherent spectral bands.

       overload
              Excessive broadband energy; unstable patterns.

       inversion-loop
              Repeated spectral inversion; mirror recursion.

       noise collapse
              Envelope dominated by noise; coherence lost.

       WRSADC detects and prevents all failure modes.

INTERACTION WITH SCHEMAS
       Schemas define:
           • allowed envelope shapes
           • spectral limits
           • sculpting rules
           • overlay compatibility

       Envelope behavior must satisfy:
           • resonance-schema
           • structural-schema
           • pattern-schema
           • constellation-schema

INTERACTION WITH LINEAGE
       Lineage records:
           • envelope snapshots
           • sculpting events
           • harmonic transitions
           • pattern-envelope correlations

       Envelope analysis depends on lineage continuity.

INTERACTION WITH WRSADC
       WRSADC:
           • computes envelope shape
           • applies shaping and sculpting
           • validates envelope-schema compliance
           • selects patterns based on envelope stability
           • blocks unsafe envelope states

       WRSADC is the envelope sculptor.

INTERACTION WITH THE ENGINE
       The Engine:
           • executes envelope-sensitive operators
           • updates internal RT-spectrum
           • integrates sculpted envelopes

       The Engine assumes envelope safety; WRSADC guarantees it.

NOTES
       Envelopes are the sculptural dimension of resonance-time. They shape
       the spectral landscape in which triads, patterns, and constellations
       operate, ensuring coherence, stability, and expressive structural
       behavior across RTT systems.

